From f7de6067547f50ab7b90c4639616fb88ed56b1e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincent Leon <leon@mbp.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:23:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] feat: search the prompts you sent from the Command
 Center

Command Center now lists "Your messages" for a query: prompts you sent in any chat on any
connected host, archived chats included, newest first. Selecting one opens its chat. Replies
are not searched.

The daemon reads prompts straight from the provider transcripts on disk (Claude Code project
transcripts, Codex rollouts under sessions/ and archived_sessions/), so no chat is resumed to
search it. Each transcript is read once and then only from where the last read stopped; the
prompts and offsets persist in prompt-search-index.json, so a restart does not reread the
history. Injected user-role content is left out: Paseo notifications, slash-command output,
system reminders, compaction summaries, the Codex AGENTS.md preamble, and chats of subagents
and background agents, whose prompts another agent wrote.

New RPC agent.prompts.search.{request,response}, gated on server_info.features.promptSearch.
